    "case_id": "458",
    "case_summary": "A patient in their 30s without any previous medical and family history presented to the emergency department because of palpitations for 14 hours. The patient reported no chest pain, shortness of breath, vertigo, or dizziness.\n\nVital signs on admission:- Temperature: 36.8°C- Blood pressure: 102/57 mm Hg- Pulse rate: 170 beats/min- Respiratory rate: 20 breaths/minResults of the physical examination were normal except for fast heart rate.\n\n- Laboratory tests:  * Troponin T: 0.018 ng/mL (reference range, <0.014 ng/mL)  * N-terminal pro-brain-type natriuretic peptide: 1709 pg/mL (reference range, <125 pg/mL)- Echocardiography findings:  * Mild enlarged left atrium (diameter: 34 mm)  * Normal left ventricle (end-diastolic diameter: 46 mm; ejection fraction: 72%)- ECG findings:  Image A Title: ECG on admission  Image A Description: Wide QRS complex tachycardia at 173 beats/min with R morphology in lead V1 and left-axis deviation. P waves in lead V1 dissociated from QRS complexes.  Image B Title: ECG at sinus rhythm  Image B Description: Third-degree atrioventricular block with ventricular rate of 48 beats/min. Narrow QS morphologies in leads V1 to V4 and widespread T-wave inversions.  Image C Title: ECG showing atrial fibrillation  Image C Description: Atrial fibrillation with ventricular rate of 46 beats/min.- Genetic testing:  * LMNA gene variant (p.Arg377Cys) identified",
